{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The enemy said.</b> Etc. When he saw the sea dried up and the deeps froze in the heart of the sea — and what did he gain? 'You blew with Your wind — the sea covered them.'" "<b>I shall draw my sword.</b> Several words are deficient in the letter bet, for example 'the widow of your father's house' (i.e., שבי for אשבי); so too here, 'I shall draw with my sword' — the bodies from the soul, the blood, and the spirit." "<b>My hand shall dispossess them.</b> A term of inheritance. <b>I shall draw my sword.</b> And I shall satisfy myself with them, and dispossess them for my people."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:59.316968358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}